# 1. EXACT PRODUCT REQUIREMENTS

## 1.1 Flexible registration

The user must be able to choose which login identifiers to provide.

Support all seven combinations:

| Registration choice | Username | Email | Phone |
|---|---|---|---|
| A | Yes | No | No |
| B | No | Yes | No |
| C | No | No | Yes |
| D | Yes | Yes | No |
| E | Yes | No | Yes |
| F | No | Yes | Yes |
| G | Yes | Yes | Yes |

The registration form must no longer require all applicants to invent a technical username.

It must not require an email when the user chooses phone registration, or require a phone when the user chooses email registration.

The user's full name and password remain separate from the chosen login identifiers.

A person's real full name must never be mistaken for a verified unique authentication identity merely because the text matches another person's name.

**Important technical constraint:** Supabase's standard password-based authentication supports email/password and phone/password. It does not automatically provide username-only password accounts.

For combination A, identify and implement a genuinely secure, supported server-backed account-authentication mechanism if one exists within the authorized local architecture and can be tested.

Do NOT manufacture internal fake email addresses, fake phone numbers, false verified identities, or browser-only username accounts.

Do NOT create an account request and falsely label it a working username/password credential.

If username-only signup and later login require an unapproved identity architecture, record that combination as BLOCKED, preserve the safely implemented combinations, and provide the exact backend decision required. Do not silently weaken the requirement.

This constraint does not excuse failing to implement the other supported cases.

## 1.2 Flexible sign-in

The user should see one clear login form:

**Sign in using your username, email or phone number**

The user enters their chosen identifier and password.

The application must support:

- A registered username and password.
- A registered email address and password.
- A registered phone number and password.
- Accounts with two registered identifiers.
- Accounts with all three registered identifiers.

When multiple identifiers are attached to the same canonical account, each eligible, verified login identifier should resolve to that same account.

Do not create separate accounts for different identifiers belonging to one person.

Do not grant school privileges merely because credentials are valid.

An unapproved account remains unable to access protected school workspaces.

**Registration using an identifier is not proof that the identifier is verified, associated with Supabase Auth, or enabled for sign-in.** This distinction must be enforced in the implementation and user feedback.

