# 4. ACTUAL SOURCE DEFECTS TO ADDRESS

The following were observed in the previously inspected GitHub source. Your latest AI Studio workspace is the implementation source of truth, so verify whether they remain before editing.

## Defect A — Forced username

`src/components/AuthModal.tsx` currently requires `username.trim()` and renders the username input as required.

That prevents email-only and phone-only registration.

The registration validation must reflect the supported identifier combinations, not require every applicant to provide a username.

## Defect B — Strict ASCII-only validation

`src/lib/username.ts` rejects spaces, Arabic and accented characters.

The database's `profiles_username_format` constraint also rejects them.

A frontend regex change alone is not sufficient.

The relevant source, database normalization/uniqueness contract, signup trigger and username lookup must agree.

If the real database schema requires a migration, prepare a separate, reviewable source migration for an isolated environment. Do not apply it to the shared live project.

Do not modify old applied migration history.

Preserve existing usernames and their ability to sign in.

## Defect C — Email/phone registration precedence

Existing `signUpAccount()` selects email/password when email is supplied, otherwise phone/password.

When the user supplies both email and phone, the second identifier is not automatically guaranteed to become a verified Supabase Auth sign-in method.

Implement or prepare the correct provider-supported linking/verification flow for the second identifier.

Both methods must point to the same canonical user.

Do not create two accounts.

Do not treat a phone recorded in a profile as a verified Auth phone identity.

If contact verification requires a separate session, OTP step or provider configuration, preserve that boundary and explain its state accurately.

## Defect D — Username login failures

Existing username sign-in uses:

```typescript
client.functions.invoke('auth-username-signin', ...)
```

The deployed Edge Function v6 returns:

```text
HTTP 401
{"error":"invalid_credentials"}
```

Supabase wraps non-2xx responses in `FunctionsHttpError`.

The correct frontend implementation must inspect the actual response status and safe error payload rather than interpreting a generic error wrapper.

Implement the transport correction so a genuine wrong password is distinguishable from a network failure, function outage, unconfirmed contact or account without an approved active role.

## Defect E — Incorrect phone normalization

Existing `normalizePhone()` prepends `+` when missing.

That can misinterpret local Tunisian phone numbers.

Make phone validation and international normalization reliable without changing already-valid registered international numbers.

## Defect F — Inconsistent identity resolution

Inspect and correct the end-to-end identity path:

```text
Registration form
    ↓
Input validation and normalization
    ↓
Supabase account creation or supported server provisioning
    ↓
Canonical profile and verified identifiers
    ↓
Requested school role, pending approval
    ↓
Email / phone / username login transport
    ↓
Real credential verification
    ↓
Canonical User.id and active-role lookup
    ↓
Authorized homepage or safe restricted-access message
```

Every connection must be backed by working code or clearly marked as not yet implemented.

Never confuse a signup request with an approved role.

